{"id":"e01eaa01-f2d0-41b2-842e-de7e3e4e01a8","object":"chat.completion","created":1793349742,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Baseline fails as expected. Now apply the three scoped edits.\n\n```python\nr1 = replace_text_batch(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", [\n {\"old_text\": \"\"\"    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n\"\"\",\n  \"new_text\": \"\"\"    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def positive_int_or_none(*, minimum: int = 32) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Optional int; unset means None, otherwise must parse as int >= minimum.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            try:\n                value = int(v)\n            except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                raise ValueError(f\"must be an integer >= {minimum}, got {v!r}\") from None\n            if value < minimum:\n                raise ValueError(f\"must be >= {minimum}, got {value}\")\n            return value\n\n        return EnvVar(_init)\n\"\"\"},\n {\"old_text\": \"\"\"    DEEPINFER_RINGBUFFER_WARNING_INTERVAL = EnvVar.int(default=60)\n\"\"\",\n  \"new_text\": \"\"\"    DEEPINFER_RINGBUFFER_WARNING_INTERVAL = EnvVar.int(default=60)\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.positive_int_or_none(minimum=32)\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"普通诊断日志消息的长度预算；未设置表示不限制。统计日志通过 keep_full_message 保留完整内容。\\\"\\\"\\\"\n\"\"\"},\n], \"fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\")\nprint(r1[\"ok\"], r1.get(\"file_hash\"))\n\nr2 = replace_text_batch(\"deepinfer/logger.py\", [\n {\"old_text\": '''_COLOR_RESET = \"\\\\033[0m\"\n''',\n  \"new_text\": '''_COLOR_RESET = \"\\\\033[0m\"\n\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n_MIN_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = 32\n''',\n },\n {\"old_text\": \"\"\"    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n\"\"\",\n  \"new_text\": \"\"\"    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= {_MIN_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS} or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n            if max_message_chars < _MIN_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS:\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be >= {_MIN_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS}, got {max_message_chars}\")\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n\n    def _truncate_message(self, message: str, budget: int) -> str:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Keep the head and tail of an over-long message, separated by a fixed marker.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        remaining = budget - len(_TRUNCATION_MARKER)\n        head_chars = (remaining + 1) // 2\n        tail_chars = remaining - head_chars\n        head = message[:head_chars]\n        tail = message[len(message) - tail_chars:] if tail_chars > 0 else \"\"\n        return f\"{head}{_TRUNCATION_MARKER}{tail}\"\n\"\"\",\n },\n {\"old_text\": \"\"\"    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\\\n\" in msg and record.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(record.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\\\n\", \"\\\\n\" + prefix)\n\"\"\",\n  \"new_text\": \"\"\"    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        target = record\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n                # 复制一份记录再替换消息，绝不改写共享原记录的 msg/args/exc_info/stack_info\n                target = logging.makeLogRecord(dict(record.__dict__))\n                target.msg = self._truncate_message(message, self.max_message_chars)\n                target.args = ()\n        msg = super().format(target)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\\\n\" in msg and target.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(target.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\\\n\", \"\\\\n\" + prefix)\n\"\"\",\n },\n {\"old_text\": \"\"\"    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n    )\n\"\"\",\n  \"new_text\": \"\"\"    from deepinfer.environ import envs\n\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )\n\"\"\",\n },\n], \"5b8f8d9947de692353609c1fc2851097d24f9b6ba6004dce1dbfa394dc6d3ec8\")\nprint(r2[\"ok\"], r2.get(\"file_hash\"))\n\nr3 = replace_text_batch(\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", [\n {\"old_text\": \"\"\"            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)\n\"\"\",\n  \"new_text\": \"\"\"            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})\n\"\"\",\n },\n], \"9ef93c3930d6dd8d889d4ba69558a85459c2210ae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9\")\nprint(r3[\"ok\"], r3.get(\"file_hash\"))\n```","reasoning_content":"Baseline done. Now I have the code I need for environ.py, logger.py, stats_logger.py. Let me check stats_logger's _log_worker full context and whether it uses extra. I have the _log_worker function lines 116-126.\n\nNow make edits.\n\nenviron.py: add `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none()`? But needs >=32 validation and error message containing var name. Note: descriptor __get__ already wraps errors with name prefix. But for ValueError... let's check: except Exception as e: try raise type(e)(f\"{self.name}: {e}\") from e; except TypeError: raise e from None. So ValueError gets re-raised with name prefix. Good.\n\nSo I can add a factory method e.g. `int_or_none(min_value=None, min_kind=...)`. Task says \"描述符类可以新增辅助工厂方法（用于创建配置项的方法）\". Let me add:\n\n```python\n    @staticmethod\n    def log_max_message_chars() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            try:\n                value = int(v)\n            except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                raise ValueError(f\"must be an integer >= 32, got {v!r}\") from None\n            if value < 32:\n                raise ValueError(f\"must be >= 32, got {value}\")\n            return value\n        return EnvVar(_init)\n```\n\nNote: `int(\"\")` raises ValueError, good. `int(\" 64 \")` works. Also need empty string -> ValueError. Yes.\n\nThen in envs:\n```python\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.log_max_message_chars()\n\"限制普通诊断日志消息长度的字符预算；未设置表示不限制。\"\n```\n\nCareful: `int` on a bool-ish string? Not relevant.\n\nlogger.py: NewLineFormatter add `max_message_chars` keyword-only param:\n\n```python\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\nclass NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter):\n    def __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars=None):\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(...)\n            if max_message_chars < 32: raise ValueError\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nWait careful with error raising: TypeError currently raised for accepting positional? Tests: test_invalid_budget[True] etc expected... They currently fail with TypeError: NewLineFormatter... meaning passing max_message_chars keyword raises TypeError (unexpected keyword). After adding keyword param they'd get ValueError presumably. Test name test_invalid_budget expects ValueError likely.\n\nNow truncation happens after argument substitution. Best approach in format(): we need record.message without mutating record. Compute the message ourselves:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        if self.max_message_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n            msg = super().format(record)\n            ... prefix logic, color\n        else:\n            truncated_message = self._truncate(record.getMessage())\n```\n\nBut `record.message` used in prefix logic. Better: use a shallow copy? Copying LogRecord via `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)`? That's a standard helper. But careful about exc_info and stack_info. Simpler: compute message text, truncate, and build formatted string via a copied record:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n        if max_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > max_chars:\n                clone = logging.makeLogRecord(dict(record.__dict__))\n                clone.msg = self._truncate(message, max_chars)\n                clone.args = ()\n                # keep message cached consistent\n                msg = super().format(clone)\n                ...\n```\n\nHmm, makeLogRecord copies __dict__ — includes exc_info, stack_info (tuples/str) fine. But record.__dict__ may contain \"message\" from a previous format; makeLogRecord sets them; then super().format will recompute message because msg/args changed? logging.Formatter.format calls record.getMessage() which sets record.message = ... So fine.\n\nActually careful: record.__dict__ contains 'exc_text' possibly None. makeLogRecord with exc_text None fine.\n\nBut simpler: avoid copying; instead compute the full formatted string then replace just the message portion. Approach: `msg = super().format(record)` gives full text including prefix and message (record.message). Then if truncated needed, replace the substring record.message with truncated version. But record.message may appear in prefix... unlikely, but the original code already uses msg.find(record.message). Hmm risky if message text also appears in prefix (e.g. filename). Use rfind? Actually safer: build via copy.\n\nLet's use the copy approach but keep the rest of format logic identical, with prefix logic using clone.message.\n\nDesign:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        record_to_format = record\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n                record_to_format = logging.makeLogRecord(dict(record.__dict__))\n                record_to_format.msg = self._truncate_message(message)\n                record_to_format.args = ()\n        msg = super().format(record_to_format)\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and record_to_format.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(record_to_format.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n        ...\n```\n\nCareful: makeLogRecord copies 'message' key from original dict if it exists (from earlier formatting). record.getMessage() when args empty and msg set... getMessage: msg = str(self.msg); if self.args: msg = msg % self.args; return msg. So message recomputed. Fine either way.\n\nAlso 'exc_text' copied; if original was formatted before, exc_text cached; fine.\n\nTruncate:\n\n```python\n    def _truncate_message(self, message: str, budget: int) -> str:\n        marker = _TRUNCATION_MARKER\n        remaining = budget - len(marker)\n        head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n        tail = remaining - head\n        return f\"{message[:head]}{marker}{message[len(message) - tail:] if tail else ''}\"\n```\n\nCheck with budget 32: marker len = len(\"...<omitted>...\") = 3+9+3 = 15. remaining = 17, head = 9, tail = 8. Matches \"保留开头9字符、末尾8字符，加上15字符标记\". Good.\n\nEdge: if remaining <= 0? budget>=32, marker 15, so remaining >=17. Fine.\n\nNote that truncation applies only when len > budget. Also must not modify exc_info/stack_info — copy keeps them; is that \"改写\"? We copy the record instead of mutating it; original untouched. Good.\n\nAlso default init: `init_logger`/`_setup_logger` must read envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS. Need import: from deepinfer.environ import envs — check logger.py imports don't import environ. Adding `from deepinfer.environ import envs` at module level might cause circular import? environ imports only stdlib. Fine. But safer to import inside _setup_logger. Let's do local import inside _setup_logger to avoid import cycle risk.\n\nIn _setup_logger:\n```python\n    from deepinfer.environ import envs\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT, use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(), max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS)\n```\n\nWait: test_independent_formatter_does_not_inherit_environment — independent formatter doesn't read env. Good since default None.\n\n\"重复初始化不能重复添加处理器\" — already handled.\n\nstats_logger: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nLet me check the full _log_worker and imports region of stats_logger to ensure context, and whether \"logger\" name is module-level (yes line 29). Read range 100-135 to confirm.\n\nAlso, need initial full reads done — yes. Phase=edit.\n\nLet me apply edits with replace_text_batch.\n\nFor environ.py, insert the factory method after int_or_none, and config item under -- Logging --.\n\nLet me write edits now.\n\nAlso read stats_logger lines 110-130 to be safe? I have 116-126 evidence; edits must match exactly. The evidence shows:\n\n```\ndef _log_worker(q: queue.SimpleQueue[list[str] | None]) -> None:\n    need_sleep = True\n    for msgs in iter(q.get, None):\n        try:\n            if need_sleep:\n                time.sleep((dist.get_rank() % 8) * 0.005)\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)\n```\n\nEdit old_text \"                logger.info(m)\\n\" → with extra. That occurrence unique enough? Might appear elsewhere. Include the for line.\n\nLet's do all three edits in one action (independent files). Also run pytest? Separate step to verify.\n\nFor logger.py file_hash 5b8f8d..., environ fe2c5..., stats 9ef93...\n\nWrite edits."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10072,"completion_tokens":3693,"total_tokens":13765,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3968},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2152},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":3968,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6104},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}